# Summary of Changes for HDDS-10926

This commit wires `ContainerChecksumTreeManager` into block deletion so that deleted blocks are recorded in the container merkle tree file.

## ContainerChecksumTreeManager.java

**Constructor** — changed to accept a `ConfigurationSource` instead of a `DatanodeConfiguration`:
```java
public ContainerChecksumTreeManager(ConfigurationSource conf) {
  fileLock = SimpleStriped.readWriteLock(
      conf.getObject(DatanodeConfiguration.class).getContainerChecksumLockStripes(), true);
  metrics = ContainerMerkleTreeMetrics.create();
}
```

**Signature generalizations** — several methods changed from `KeyValueContainerData` to the parent `ContainerData`:
- `writeContainerDataTree(ContainerData data, ContainerMerkleTree tree)`
- `read(ContainerData data)`
- `write(ContainerData data, ContainerProtos.ContainerChecksumInfo checksumInfo)`

**markBlocksAsDeleted** — parameter loosened from `SortedSet<Long>` to `Collection<Long>`:
```java
public void markBlocksAsDeleted(KeyValueContainerData data, Collection<Long> deletedBlockIDs) throws IOException {
```
Internally it still sorts and deduplicates via a `TreeSet` (a comment noting the input was already sorted was removed).

**getContainerChecksumFile** — made `static` and generalized to `ContainerData`:
```java
public static File getContainerChecksumFile(ContainerData data) {
  return new File(data.getMetadataPath(), data.getContainerID() + ".tree");
}
```

## ContainerData.java

Added an abstract method so metadata path is available on the base class:
```java
public abstract String getMetadataPath();
```
(`KeyValueContainerData.getMetadataPath()` now carries `@Override`.)

## BlockDeletingService.java

A field was added: `private final ContainerChecksumTreeManager checksumTreeManager;`

**Constructors:**
```java
// @VisibleForTesting convenience constructor
public BlockDeletingService(OzoneContainer ozoneContainer, long serviceInterval,
    long serviceTimeout, TimeUnit timeUnit, int workerSize, ConfigurationSource conf) {
  this(ozoneContainer, serviceInterval, serviceTimeout, timeUnit, workerSize,
      conf, "", new ContainerChecksumTreeManager(conf), null);
}

// full constructor — now takes the tree manager
public BlockDeletingService(OzoneContainer ozoneContainer, long serviceInterval,
    long serviceTimeout, TimeUnit timeUnit, int workerSize, ConfigurationSource conf,
    String threadNamePrefix, ContainerChecksumTreeManager checksumTreeManager,
    ReconfigurationHandler reconfigurationHandler) {
  super("BlockDeletingService", serviceInterval, timeUnit, workerSize, serviceTimeout, threadNamePrefix);
  this.ozoneContainer = ozoneContainer;
  this.checksumTreeManager = checksumTreeManager;
  ...
}
```

The `BlockDeletingTaskBuilder` gained a field and setter, and passes the manager to the task:
```java
public BlockDeletingTaskBuilder setChecksumTreeManager(ContainerChecksumTreeManager treeManager) {
  this.checksumTreeManager = treeManager;
  return this;
}
// build():
new BlockDeletingTask(blockDeletingService, containerBlockInfo, checksumTreeManager, priority);
```

## BlockDeletingTask.java

New field `private final ContainerChecksumTreeManager checksumTreeManager;` set in the constructor:
```java
public BlockDeletingTask(BlockDeletingService blockDeletingService,
    BlockDeletingService.ContainerBlockInfo containerBlockInfo,
    ContainerChecksumTreeManager checksumTreeManager, int priority) {
  ...
  this.checksumTreeManager = checksumTreeManager;
}
```

The inner `ContainerBackgroundTaskResult` switched its list from `String` block names to `Long` block IDs (`addBlockId(Long)`, `addAll(List<Long>)`, `getDeletedBlocks()` returning `List<Long>`).

## How markBlocksAsDeleted is called

The task now tracks both block IDs and DB keys separately (`succeedBlockIDs` and `succeedBlockDBKeys`). Per the code comments, this is done "before the delete transactions are removed from the database" so reconciliation can skip copying deleted block data.

Two call sites:
```java
// deleteViaSchema... path
checksumTreeManager.markBlocksAsDeleted(containerData, succeedBlockIDs);

// transaction-based path
checksumTreeManager.markBlocksAsDeleted(containerData, crr.getDeletedBlocks());
```

## OzoneContainer.java wiring

`OzoneContainer` creates the shared manager and injects it:
```java
checksumTreeManager = new ContainerChecksumTreeManager(config);
...
new BlockDeletingService(..., config, datanodeDetails.threadNamePrefix(),
    checksumTreeManager, context.getParent().getReconfigurationHandler());
```
On shutdown it also calls `ContainerMerkleTreeMetrics.unregister();` (that method was made `static`).

